Reading (12 October 2026): only three relations are strong. Gloss is Roughness inverted (exact), Specular is a linear Remap of Cavity (0.988, a ceiling that no nonlinearity or extra map lifts), and Bump is a band filter of the displacement (0.988, but only from the reference displacement). Cavity and the Normal are NOT derivable from the 2K displacement or bump: their pixel-scale content comes from a source the 2K height does not contain (the 8K scan), so they are independent maps at pixel level. (12 October 2026)

Band variance shares (12 October 2026): Cavity has 56 percent of its variance below 1 px, Specular 59 percent, Bump 53 percent, NormalR 34 percent, Displacement 0.3 percent. (12 October 2026)

JPEG check (12 October 2026): the Specular residual after a*Cavity+b is 2.42 percent of its variance, the 8-bit quantisation explains 0.45 percent; the step across 8x8 block boundaries is 0.92 to 1.01 times the inner step for every map, so the residual is real fine content, not block artefacts. Chasing it is not chasing compression noise. (12 October 2026)

