Key point (12 October 2026): the Cavity residual is dense, not sparse. 35 percent of all pixels must be stored to reach 0.99, and coarser cells cannot reach it at all (2x2 cells over the whole image stop at 0.872). The dark cracks and specks are not few isolated outliers: they are a dense grain, so no sparse representation exists. Correcting Specular through the Cavity works because both share positions: at Cavity 0.995 the Specular Remap needs only 26 169 extra points. (12 October 2026)

